  "description": "that I'd be able to buy a\nreal (non-department store, that is) dual suspension mountain bike for\nless than half a grand, I would have chuckled. I sell cross-country skis\nthat cost nearly that, and they don't have any moving parts at all!\n\nThe Discovery 2 slips under the wire by using the Discovery 3's main triangle\nof 7005 aluminum mated to a cro-moly steel rear triangle that's plenty\nstiff, although slightly heavier than its aluminum counterpart. Front\nbumps are tamed with 65mm of SunTour XCE fork travel. And you can still\nlook forward, even at this price, to 3.3\" of rear axle travel suspended\nby a coil spring shock. Eight speed shifting has also trickled down to\nthis price range so you'll never feel like the gear you want is the nonexistent\none between the two you have.\n\nI see you riding the Discovery 2 on the carriage paths of Bar Harbor,\nMaine. Or along the beach bike path in Costa Mesa, CA. Or maybe you've\nbeen wondering where that unpaved rail trail near your house leads. You\ndon't need an endless backcountry to have a mountain bike adventure. You\njust need a bike. And nobody's deducting points for going in comfort and\nstyle. So have at it.",
